      "writtenOn": "2018-01-12T00:35:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "since this is so easy for people to pass in as their fallback value, I wonder if a better default for a nil fallback is redirecting http to https, at least for GET/HEAD requests?\n\nI\u0027m curious what others think.\n\nAlso, if LetsEncrypt is shutting down tls-sni-{01,02} for good, maybe we should do even more magic in this package.\n\nIf this HTTPHandler method was never called, we could optimistically try to open port 80 and hope for the best and use it if we get it? The risk is that there\u0027s a firewall or proxies in front of us and port 80 requests never get to us. But it might fix a good chunk of people without any changes to their code.\n\nI also wonder whether we could add something to net/http + the standard library to route these http-01 ACME challenges to the autocert or autocert-like packages, without the user explicitly wiring them. I\u0027m thinking of a pretty safe way to do it, repeating such requests if the default handler ends up replying with a 404.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 253,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 253,
        "endChar": 35
      },
